  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Steppin'** (1 review): Around minute four the band eases into Relax, from Lettuce's latest release, fully there by 5:40, then returns to Steppin' near 7:28 [3]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Don't Worry About Me**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [6]\n- **I'll Never Know**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 4 archived performances [6]\n- **A Song For You**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 5 archived performances [6]\n- **Swamp**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 6 archived performances [6]\n- **Prototype**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [6]\n- **Relax**: rare: 4 archived performances [6]\n- **James Brown medley: Lickin' Stick/There Was A Time**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [6]\n- **goodnights**: back after 240 archived shows (3597 days); rare: 3 archived performances [6]\n- Earliest performances in the archive: For Granted, Too Much [6]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **soulive2009-04-16** (recommended): audience recording; 16 songs; 122 min; rated 2.5/5 by 2 [1]. Said about its sound: Reviewer says the taper did a high-quality job with the audience recording [3]\n- **soulive2009-04-16.flac24**: audience recording; 14 songs; 122 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- The show was the New York album release party for \"Up Here\" [1]\n- Sam Kininger and Ryan Zoidas joined as the \"Shady Horns\" on some songs; Nigel Hall sang on others [1]\n- New York album release party for \"Up Here\", with the Shady Horns (Kininger, Zoidas) and Nigel Hall on vocals on marked songs [2]\n- Reviewer feels the band returned to its roots, with horns and instrumentals, and found Nigel's vocal contributions unnecessary [3]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **soulive2009-04-16**: taped by Scott Bernstein; transferred by Scott Bernstein; source: Audience [1]. Also: Scott Bernstein recorded, mastered and tracked this recording; a higher-quality 24-bit version is posted separately [1]\n- **soulive2009-04-16.flac24**: taped by Scott Bernstein; transferred by Scott Bernstein; source: Audience [2]. Also: Scott Bernstein recorded, mastered and tracked the show. This is a 24-bit fileset, not meant for CD burning; A separate 16-bit version with MP3 and streaming is available on archive.org [2]",
